 # Changelog
+
+## v1.1.0
+
+- Add first-class Linux agent telemetry while preserving the existing Windows agent protocol and server compatibility.
+- Read Linux CPU utilization from `/proc/stat`, memory pressure from `/proc/meminfo`, and host uptime from `/proc/uptime`.
+- Monitor systemd services through a bounded `systemctl show` query and normalize common Linux service states to the existing OpsForge service-state model.
+- Keep HTTP, TCP, DNS, process, drive, network, authentication, mTLS, tracing, correlation, and fleet-service identity behavior shared across Windows and Linux.
+- Add a Linux example configuration, publish helper, hardened systemd unit, and installer.
+- Preserve Windows `ServiceController`, `GetSystemTimes`, and `GlobalMemoryStatusEx` behavior without changing the server heartbeat contract.

 ## v1.0.0
